SUMMARY:[AI ADJUSTED] running — 60 min pool swim\, 2\,000m at 2:30/100m: 
 400m warm-up\, 8×100m 
DESCRIPTION:60 min pool swim\, 2\,000m at 2:30/100m: 400m warm-up\, 8×100m
  @ 2:25/100m with 15-sec rest (rather than 6×200m) to build interval tole
 rance more gradually\, 400m cool-down — this session label should be cor
 rected to 'swimming' in the plan.\n\nReason: The session is labelled as a 
 Sunday Long Run but contains swim content\, and restructuring the interval
 s to 8×100m rather than 6×200m is more appropriate for an athlete rebuil
 ding swim fitness toward a 5000m open-water race 7 weeks from this date.\n
 \nAI coaching 2026-08-01
