SUMMARY:[AI ADJUSTED] swimming — 60 min open-water sea swim\, 2\,000m at 
 2:25–2:30/100m as plan
DESCRIPTION:60 min open-water sea swim\, 2\,000m at 2:25–2:30/100m as pla
 nned — add one sighting-buoy navigation drill every 400m (lift eyes ever
 y 8–10 strokes) to begin building the open-water race skills needed for 
 the Half Oceanman 5000m course.\n\nReason: The Half Oceanman is an open-wa
 ter event and sighting efficiency under fatigue is a trainable skill that 
 is best introduced progressively from week 9 onward rather than left to ra
 ce week.\n\nAI coaching 2026-08-01
END:VEVENT
