 p\, 3×1\,000m @ 2:28/1
DESCRIPTION:75 min pool race-simulation: 500m warm-up\, 3×1\,000m @ 2:28/1
 00m with 60-sec rest (total 3\,000m working set)\, 200m cool-down — this
  is the key Half Oceanman fitness marker and should be treated as a B-prio
 rity race effort\; wear the race wetsuit if available to simulate race con
 ditions.\n\nReason: With the Half Oceanman 63 days away and no specific 3\
 ,000m+ continuous swim block yet in the plan\, introducing a structured 3
 ×1\,000m set at race pace on this Friday gives the clearest fitness signa
 l and the most race-specific stimulus at the right time in the build.\n\nA
 I coaching 2026-08-01
